{"chunk_id": "d90f6ac685f8", "text": "Pandu tells Kunti that the lord of the gods has been pleased by her vow and will grant her a son of unmatched valor. Following his request, Kunti invokes Sakra (Indra), who fathers the child later known as Arjuna. At Arjuna\u2019s birth, a divine voice proclaims his future greatness: he will rival legendary heroes, defeat powerful enemies, aid the Kurus, burn the Khandava forest to satisfy Agni, obtain celestial weapons including Shiva\u2019s Pasupata, and even destroy the fearsome Nivatakavacha demons. The event is celebrated by an immense gathering of gods, sages, Gandharvas, Apsaras, Nagas, and other celestial beings who rejoice and shower blessings upon the newborn. Afterwards Pandu desires more children, but Kunti refuses, citing scriptural limits and social norms regarding multiple partners.\nKunti invokes Indra and gives birth to Arjuna, whose divine destiny is proclaimed as gods and sages celebrate his birth.\nThemes: divine birth, prophecy of heroism, cosmic celebration, Kshatriya destiny", "vector": [0.013933293521404266, -0.0246481541544199, -0.013443243689835072, 0.022012483328580856, -0.005056116729974747, 0.013218086212873459, -0.016635186970233917, 0.007734831888228655, -0.02531038410961628, -0.015880245715379715, 0.0061852168291807175, 0.007350739557296038, -0.002117476426064968, -0.0002203980111517012, -0.009569205343723297, 0.023244230076670647, 0.04251508787274361, -0.016873588785529137, 0.02987976185977459, -0.02074100449681282, -0.014317385852336884, -0.004734935704618692, 0.01188038382679224, 0.015694821253418922, -0.02932349033653736, 0.029906250536441803, 0.011827405542135239, -0.023615077137947083, 0.016039181500673294, 0.00018749352602753788, -0.021760838106274605, 0.014622011221945286, -0.00249991356395185, -0.004268064629286528, -0.032369744032621384, -0.005966681055724621, -0.004291242454200983, -0.01927085779607296, 0.009039422497153282, 0.002135687740519643, 0.020370157435536385, -0.011628736741840